Current:
-------
- support SQLRelay http://sqlrelay.sf.net (only available for Unix)
- add placemarkers for MySQL
- add Oracle8 OCI support

For Rexx/SQL 3.0
----------------
- new connect function: sqlconnectex() same as sqlconnect() but has first option as database
  connection type, plus extra database-specific options
- split into rexxsql.dll and rexx???.dll
  where rexxsql.dll determines which database drivers are available by attempting
  to load each database specific dll
  - globally have array of external function pointers to the appropriate
    database specific dll function pointers
- sequence of events
  - sqlloadfuncs() registers all sql???() functions which are all wrappers for
    the database-specific functions. it also determines which rexx/sql drivers are
    available by dlopen() on each known dll and stores address of DLL in TLD
  - sqlconnect() with no extra arg will check if more than 1 rexx/sql dll exists; if
    so exits with error (can't determine which database type connection is for)
    if extra arg, check that dll is available, if not error. if exists, then load all
    exports from dll into TLD array, and call ???loadfuncs() to register all functions (and call any
    database initialisation), then call ???connect()
  - sqlcommand() for example, looks up ???command() from TLD which contains pointers to
    the current database-specific dll external functions, then calls ???command()
  - sqldropfuncs() calls each non-null (in TLD array) ???dropfuncs() function.
- existing rexx???.dll to behave independent of rexxsql.dll and operate the same way as it
  currently does
- building:
  configure will need to find each database that is installed
  need a Makefile in each database dir, so we have ora/Makefile.in (and ora/vcwin32.mak)
